cache-clock

Based on cache-clock 0.3.0, part of the "benai-mods" Claude Code mods collection
by Ben AI (https://www.benai.co). Redistributed in joel/skill-marketplace with
the author's permission.

Changes from 0.3.0 (in 0.4.0):
- The ~/.claude/mods/switches.json switches (from benai's `mods` pane) are
  gone. The mod is turned off with `/plugin disable cache-clock`; Hide and
  `/cacheclock hide` apply to the current chat only.
- The home directory is read from HOME ($.env.get).
- bin/ttl.py (python3) became hooks/ttl.ts: the cache length is read from the
  end of the chat's transcript with `tail`, at the path the engine's Stop hook
  gives.
- A handoff request the handoff mod does not take within 7 s is removed, and
  the band says the handoff mod is not running.
- When its one row would wrap, the band uses three short rows instead.
- Tests were rewritten to match the changes above.
Everything else is the upstream code.

Changes in 0.5.0:
- The clock starts at each main-thread request (turn.step), not at the end of
  the turn. The approach is adapted from ribbon by Jay E / RoboNuggets
  (https://github.com/robonuggets/ribbon), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2026 Jay E | RoboNuggets (robonuggets.com).

Changes in 0.6.0:
- A resumed or forked chat seeds the clock from classic.SessionStart, and
  /clear and /compact drop it, also adapted from ribbon (see 0.5.0).

Changes in 0.7.0:
- The band prices the next message in dollars (hooks/price.ts), an idea
  from ribbon (see 0.5.0). The prices and the 5 min / 1 hour write
  multipliers are Anthropic's published list prices, not ribbon's table.
